<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gombodorj</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1594">1594</a>–<a href="/years/1655">1655</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Tüsheet Khan Gombodorj</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gombodorj was Tüsheet Khan, ruler of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, in the first half of the 17th century, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abtai-sain-khan">Abtai Sain Khan</a>. He is best known as the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanabazar">Zanabazar</a>, whom the Khalkha nobility recognised as a reincarnate lama in 1639 and who became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebtsundamba-khutughtu">Jebtsundamba Khutughtu</a>, and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chakhundorj">Chakhundorj</a>, who succeeded him as Tüsheet Khan. His reign saw the Khalkha drawn into relations with the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> state.</p></div>
